[NeilGirdhar 2023-12-19] Respecting the metaclass' `__call__` return type is required to type check [nnx](https://github.com/google/flax/tree/main/flax/experimental/nnx), which makes extensive use of this feature [here](https://github.com/google/flax/blob/f1cb0114a3aacefd28676cc6796613c916788af8/flax/experimental/nnx/nnx/variables.py#L89).
---
[Viicos 2023-12-20] > Respecting the metaclass' `__call__` return type is required to type check [nnx](https://github.com/google/flax/tree/main/flax/experimental/nnx), which makes extensive use of this feature [here](https://github.com/google/flax/blob/f1cb0114a3aacefd28676cc6796613c916788af8/flax/experimental/nnx/nnx/variables.py#L89).

As a workaround, I'm using the `__new__`  method instead (see https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/16020#issuecomment-1761244557, where I'm hitting the same use case as you)
