[jorenham 2025-02-28] This is also a blocker for correctly annotating the `numpy.object_` constructor, as well as the constructors of (all) other scalar types in case of "multidimensional" input:

```pycon
>>> import numpy as np
>>> type(np.object_(42))
<class 'int'>
>>> np.float16([3.14, 6.28])
array([3.14, 6.28], dtype=float16)
```

See https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/18343#issuecomment-2571784915 for details.
